# @marcmouries/lilyjs is published privately to GitHub Packages (the lilyJS repo
# is private, and a GitHub Packages npm package inherits its repository's
# visibility), so installing it requires authentication.
#
# This file carries the SCOPE MAPPING ONLY — deliberately no _authToken line.
# A project .npmrc SHADOWS ~/.npmrc, so a line like
#   //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
# overrides a developer's real token with an empty string whenever that variable
# is unset, and the install fails 401 with no hint why. Measured, not guessed.
#
# Supply the token per environment instead:
#   local dev  — one line in ~/.npmrc:
#                  //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=<PAT with read:packages>
#                (e.g. gh auth refresh -s read:packages, then gh auth token)
#   CI/deploy  — the workflow appends the same line using secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN;
#                the package must also grant this repo access under
#                "Manage Actions access", since GITHUB_TOKEN is scoped to the
#                repository running the workflow and lilyJS is a different one.
@marcmouries:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
